# Windows batch files must have CRLF line endings.
#
# CMD's multi-line `if (...) else (...)` blocks and `goto :label` jumps are a
# known parsing hazard with LF-only files, and this project has already shipped
# two Windows batch regressions. `core.autocrlf` would cover a git clone but not
# a ZIP download from GitHub — which is the documented install path — so pin it
# here, where it applies to both.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Everything else stays LF so the shell scripts work on macOS and Linux.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

*.png binary
